metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-5 = cons "## Stateboxes: processes as the substance" (cons "" (cons "Carl Adam Petri's dissertation of 1962 described concurrent processes as nets: places holding tokens, transitions consuming and producing them. A net's state is a marking; its behavior is every sequence of firings. In 1990 José Meseguer and Ugo Montanari showed that the executions of a Petri net form a monoidal category: firings compose in sequence and in parallel, and a process is an arrow. Statebox (Jelle Herold, Fabrizio Genovese and their team in Amsterdam) took that result as a programming language: a program is a net, its runs are the arrows of the free symmetric monoidal category the net generates, and programs compose by gluing nets at their boundaries. John Baez saw it as an attempt at a universal language of distributed systems." (cons "" (cons "My own line arrives at the same substance from practice. At Citadel Securities, with Gašper Ažman, a contributor to the C++ standards committee from whom I learned the craft of programming languages, I built a language for arbitrary protocols that generated optimal reactive parsers: a protocol is a state machine, a message is a firing, and the code that runs it is derived from its specification. In hyperactivity the same substance is the handler construction of §7.6: a computation is a tree of commands and continuations, and a handler gives each command its meaning. The firm as one program is a statebox: its fleet, its research and its people one composed process whose risk bounds are invariants of the whole. The workflow is a statebox: its nodes are conditions, work is the flow of tokens, and a node resolves when a marking witnesses its statement. Consciousness is one continuous loop with no turns: a statebox that never stops firing." (cons "" (cons "The words that follow carry this substance on: they give a process an identity that is its behavior, an account of what it receives, and a home inside the system that runs it." (cons "" nil)))))))
